camellia-key-bits-unmarshal: accept the implemented Camellia key sizes in TPMI_CAMELLIA_KEY_BITS

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2, "TPMI_!ALG.S_KEY_BITS" (Table: the
TPM_KEY_BITS interface types of the symmetric algorithms)):

  "TPMI_CAMELLIA_KEY_BITS ... Allowed Values {128, 192, 256}"

TPMI_CAMELLIA_KEY_BITS admits every Camellia key size the TPM implements
(here CAMELLIA_128 and CAMELLIA_256 of TpmProfile_Common.h); upstream
hard-codes 128, so a Camellia-256 symmetric definition (TPM2_TestParms, a
SYMCIPHER key, the symmetric algorithm of a storage key or of a session) is
rejected with TPM_RC_VALUE although Camellia-256 is implemented.

diff --git a/src/Unmarshal.c b/src/Unmarshal.c
--- a/src/Unmarshal.c
+++ b/src/Unmarshal.c
@@ -2700,19 +2700,31 @@
 TPMI_CAMELLIA_KEY_BITS_Unmarshal(TPMI_CAMELLIA_KEY_BITS *target, BYTE **buffer, INT32 *size)
 {
     TPM_RC rc = TPM_RC_SUCCESS;
 
     if (rc == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) {
 	rc = TPM_KEY_BITS_Unmarshal(target, buffer, size);
     }
     if (rc == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) {
 	switch (*target) {
+	  // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+	  // TPMI_CAMELLIA_KEY_BITS admits the implemented key sizes (Part 2,
+	  // "$CAMELLIA_KEY_SIZES_BITS"); upstream hard-codes 128 although the
+	  // profile implements CAMELLIA_256 (and CAMELLIA_192 when enabled).
+#if CAMELLIA_128
 	  case 128:
+#endif
+#if CAMELLIA_192
+	  case 192:
+#endif
+#if CAMELLIA_256
+	  case 256:
+#endif
 	    break;
 	  default:
 	    rc = TPM_RC_VALUE;
 	}
     }
     return rc;
 }
 #endif
 
